From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] platform: Keep a GtkApplicationWindow from making a second
 menubar

On Wayland the module gives a GtkApplicationWindow's application a
menubar model, and puts each GtkMenuBar realized in the window into it.
Where gtk-shell-shows-menubar is off, as it is while nothing owns
com.canonical.AppMenu.Registrar, the window makes a GtkMenuBar of its own
from the application's menubar. That one is realized in the same window,
so it went into the model it was made from, and each item it got became
another change of the model. The program never got out of showing its
window: pluma and atril started with the module and no registrar showed
nothing at all.

Turn the window's show-menubar off where the application had no menubar
of its own. All the model then has is the window's menubars, and those
are in the window already.
---
 subprojects/appmenu-gtk-module/src/platform.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/subprojects/appmenu-gtk-module/src/platform.c b/subprojects/appmenu-gtk-module/src/platform.c
index 2e5ff92..b0476ea 100644
--- a/subprojects/appmenu-gtk-module/src/platform.c
+++ b/subprojects/appmenu-gtk-module/src/platform.c
@@ -333,6 +333,13 @@ G_GNUC_INTERNAL WindowData *gtk_wayland_window_get_window_data(GtkWindow *window
 			gtk_application_set_menubar(GTK_APPLICATION(application),
 			                            G_MENU_MODEL(window_data->menu_model));
 
+			// Where no shell shows the menubar, the window would make one of its
+			// own from that model, and the model would take that one in as well.
+			if (old_menu_model == NULL)
+				gtk_application_window_set_show_menubar(GTK_APPLICATION_WINDOW(
+				                                            window),
+				                                        FALSE);
+
 			g_free(unity_object_path);
 		}
 		else
